  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **James Speaks**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2015-08-03.spyder9.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 22 songs; 140 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The venue opened in 1951 as Miami Beach Municipal Auditorium and was renamed for Jackie Gleason in 1987 [1]\n- From 1966 to 1970 the venue hosted Jackie Gleason's CBS television show [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2015-08-03.spyder9.flac16**: taped by Dan Nolan, Jr. - spyder9; transferred by Dan Nolan, Jr. - spyder9; source: Nakamichi CM-1000 CP-101 (OEM) > Naiant Littlebox (V1 Jenson) > Sony PCM-M10 (24/44.1) [1]. Also: Spyder9 Studios taped, transferred and edited the recording, taped from general admission orchestra, row A, directly front-center [1]",
